in this day and age of rapid-fire  frame-by-frame analysis there's not much  that goes unnoticed in modern movies  secretly I'm just like hey man where is  the chase and how do I cut to it but  there have been some cinematic Easter  eggs that were so subtle they slipped  right by us until years later when  eagle-eyed fans finally spotted  something new in film favorites here are  a few movie Easter eggs that went  unnoticed for a surprisingly long time  go Red Wings  it took decades for one not so minor  detail from John Hughes's 1986  existential comedy Ferris Bueller's Day  Off to finally be explained in the movie  teen slacker Ferris takes his girlfriend  Sloane his best friend Cameron on a  senior skip day adventure through  Chicago together the trio hits some of  the Windy City's most iconic sites  including Wrigley Field and The Art  Institute of Chicago all the while  Cameron wore a Detroit Red Wings hockey  jersey which is nothing short of  blasphemy since the team is an old rival  of the Chicago Blackhawks it wasn't  until the film's 30th anniversary  celebration in 2016 that the reason for  cams peculiar thread selection was  finally revealed actor Alan ruck  explained that his iconic shirt was  actually a nod to the friction he had  with his dad in the movie ruck said that  the director quote decided Cameron had a  horrible relationship with his father  but a great relationship with his  grandfather who lived in Detroit and  could take Cameron to Red Wings games  that's all it was and it was never  explained the movie  holy Groot in late 2015  guardians of the galaxy director James  Gunn revealed cut image from the movie  on his Facebook page in which his  animated tree hero Groot resided over a  table full of characters arranged just  like Leonardo da Vinci's the Last Supper  after one fan joked that group could be  his own cross because he's a tree and  thusly made of wood Gunn mentioned that  the fan wasn't far off and there was a  similarly Christ themed Easter egg that  fans had not yet noticed then someone  found it as the team ship is about to  crash Groot stretches his arms out in a  shape resembling Christ on the cross  shielding the other guardians which is a  pretty christ-like gesture as well  think about it medication memo Hannibal  Lector is definitely had his share  memorable moments over the years  arguably the most memorable of all came  in Silence of the Lambs when he told  Clarice Starling about another  government official who tried to match  wits with him a census taker once tried  to test me I ate his liver with some  fava beans and a nice Chianti it may not  have been obvious to everyone but that  maniacal menu description might have  contained a sinister clue see the movie  was based on Thomas Harris's 1988 novel  of the same name which was published at  a time when a certain antidepressant was  popularly prescribed that medication  known as an MAOI just so happened to  have advised against patients ingesting  items eerily similar to the ones he  described namely foods like liver fava  beans and red wine Hannibal himself  would have known this since he was a  psychiatrist so maybe he was giving  Clarice a hint that he'd gone off his  meds and planned his big escape from the  cell that separated him from the rest of  the world the potato strikes back the  Star Wars franchise might just be the  most-watched in history  needless to say over the years keen eyes  have spotted occasional gaffes mistakes  and an in-joke until the making of the  Empire Strikes Back  push the cast and crew to their limits  George Lucas wanting a break from  directing and daunted by the pressure of  following up Star Wars might not have  directed the sequel but he still took a  hands-on approach during the production  process especially when it came to the  special effects the film's famed  asteroid chase became a particular  sticking point for Lucas who reportedly  ordered the effects crew to redo it  several times bored frustrated and  inspired by a passing comment remarking  that the asteroids look like potatoes  the effects team decided to hide an  actual potato in an asteroid field  during a chase scene I think Ken Ralston  said ah hell looks like a potato just  put some potatoes and so they once in  the very distant very distance were  actual potatoes  Lucas himself apparently didn't notice  the prank until years later  audiences took their time - it wasn't  until the days of video and laserdisc  that viewers could freeze frame the  scene in place bought the spud thanks  for watching  subscribe to our YouTube channel for  more videos like the one you just  watched  and let us know which little-known  Easter eggs you've noticed in movies
 

